Direction queue: store up to 2 queued. When applying tick: 
```
function step(){
  const next = queue.shift();
  if (next) dir = next;
  const head = {x: snake[0].x+dir.x, y: snake[0].y+dir.y};
  if (head.x<0||head.x>=COLS||head.y<0||head.y>=ROWS) return gameOver();
  // self collision: eating case — tail moves away unless growing
  const willGrow = head.x===food.x && head.y===food.y;
  const body = willGrow ? snake : snake.slice(0, -1);
  if (body.some(s=>s.x===head.x&&s.y===head.y)) return gameOver();
  snake.unshift(head);
  if (willGrow) { score += 10; food = spawnFood(); } else snake.pop();
}
```

Queue validation: when pushing, compare against last queued dir (or dir if queue empty); reject if opposite or same.

```
function pushDir(nd){
  const last = queue.length ? queue[queue.length-1] : dir;
  if (nd.x === -last.x && nd.y === -last.y) return;
  if (nd.x === last.x && nd.y === last.y) return;
  if (queue.length < 2) queue.push(nd);
}
```

spawnFood: collect free cells, pick random. 400 cells, fine.

Loop with rAF:
```
let acc=0, last=0;
function frame(t){
  if(!last) last=t;
  const dt = Math.min(t-last, 250); last=t;
  if(state==='playing'){ acc+=dt; const iv=tickInterval(); while(acc>=iv){acc-=iv; step(); if(state!=='playing')break;} }
  draw();
  requestAnimationFrame(frame);
}
```

